# Vendored, and byte-identity is the point.
#
# docs/story-maps/story-map.css is installed verbatim by the upstream
# @windyroad/itil story-map renderer. It is committed because the maps are
# committed artefacts and render unstyled without it.
#
# lint-staged runs `prettier --write` over `*.{json,css,md}`, and this file is
# NOT in prettier's output shape (it packs several declarations per line), so
# without this entry every commit would rewrite it. That matters at the next
# plugin upgrade: a reformatted local copy turns each re-render into a 195-line
# whitespace diff, and a real upstream change — a contrast fix, a focus-ring
# change — becomes invisible inside it. Byte-identical means an unchanged
# upstream emits an EMPTY diff and a changed one emits a readable diff.
#
# Do not edit the file. Edit it upstream and re-render.
docs/story-maps/story-map.css

# ADR-053 phase 1 — the imported website tree.
#
# lint-staged runs `"*.{json,css,md}": "prettier --write"` with no path scope, so
# without this entry the FIRST thing it does is reformat every .css/.json/.md the
# import carries — inside the one commit that must stay reviewable. ADR-046's Bad
# consequence ("Every move surfaces lint debt") predicts exactly this.
#
# Paired with the ESLint ignore in eslint.config.js. Both are phase 1 only.
